WEBVTT

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.910
"Ministry of Fairies"

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.910
Come in.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.410
Pardon us.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.790
An art dealer named Hellner Falk
was keeping <i>Black Three</i> hidden,

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:31.910
and Bran Segaia, who runs a
shipping firm in Fuzan, had <i>Black Six</i> .

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.160
Will you confirm them now?

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.200
No, I shall examine them later.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.500
You two, go back and see to your duties.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.160
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.700
Understood.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.000
Of Gui Carlin's four top executives,
only the Eyes remain.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.620
Eajey has <i>Black Nine</i> .

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.620
And he's operating out of Theodolua,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.080
the abandoned castle where
His Imperial Majesty once was.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.290
Yes.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.120
We arrested Vice-Minister Nick Reimer,
of the Foreign Affairs Ministry.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:13.950
So I heard. I never expected a
traitor within our own government.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.870
Is he the only one?

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.160
What are you saying?

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.870
The report that the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i>
had been discovered at the port island

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.950
was delivered to both the Ministries
of Foreign Affairs and Fairies.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:29.040
That's because stationed on the island is a
Foreign Affairs Ministry administrator,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.200
as well as a Fairy Ministry inspector.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.580
We think the information leaked
from the Foreign Affairs Ministry.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.450
But it could also have been
the Ministry of Fairies.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.040
Surely you don't suspect <i>us</i> ?

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.870
It's a possibility. I just want to use
this chance to expel all corruption.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.000
Agreed. I will thoroughly
investigate my entire staff.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.370
Please do.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.290
Corruption, eh?

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.450
"Episode 18"
"Dancing Mouse and Broken Horn"

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.450
"Abandoned castle of Theodolua"

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.290
Nearest to the Original Fairy...

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.370
The holy beast, equal to God...

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.540
Fairy possession...

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.700
This means Colen Thor didn't make all the
contents of the Midend epigraphs public.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.250
He was your ancestor, right, Master Eajey?

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.790
Yes.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.410
And a sensible ancestor, at that.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:12.660
People are foolish. If everyone in the
world was me, no one would suffer.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.620
The transplant was successful?

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.870
Yes, sir. No issues.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.870
How many rats does that make?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:24.450
Including me, he is the 54th
Cultivated Fairy Soldier.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.870
So, we're finally at about fifty-fifty.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:33.700
The precision of the transplant procedure
should improve, the more we perform.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.250
Keep adding to their number.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:40.200
And keep dumping the corpses of
transplant failures in the sewer.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.790
"Dorothea HQ"

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.040
Hold down the fort. Help out the director.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.000
Sure, I've got this.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.250
Robert.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.250
We'll be back!

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.250
Yup. Take care.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.750
We'll be fine!

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.450
Because I'll be with them.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.790
That just makes me worry more.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.620
There you go again.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.450
Ready?

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.540
Yes, sir.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:32.540
It's rather cozy here.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.200
I appreciate your thoughtfulness.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.750
We just want to do all we can
to conceal your existence.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.830
Certainly.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.620
I especially want to keep
Marco Bellwood from knowing.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.080
How much do you know about him?

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:55.950
The descendant of Hel S. Bellwood, the first
fairy scholar and creator of the Fairy Tome.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.870
It goes without saying the Bellwoods
are a distinguished family.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:04.370
Marco was known from a young age to be
a very learned and talented fairy scholar.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:12.000
And before unification was achieved, he served
Golbarn Helwise, who was still king of Cidal.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.580
There's nothing strange about that.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.870
Every nation was focused at that time
on the technological development

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.700
of artificial fairies and Fairy Soldiers.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.120
Cidal was particularly proactive.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:28.750
Yes. The <i>Blue Fairy Tome</i> author Jay B. Mercer's
descendant works for him as well.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:33.080
Griff Mercer. He's Marco
Bellwood's right-hand man.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.500
And, they're trying to assemble
the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.750
By the way, do you know of a
religious order called Eins?

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.080
Eins...

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:49.040
O Original Fairy, progenitor of all things.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:55.870
All impurity shall be wiped away,
and the ideal world shall soon emerge.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:07:00.450
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:04.540
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:08.750
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.410
Here we are.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:25.750
Tell me why we came all the way to Mazria?

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:30.290
Well, Eajey is in that abandoned
castle of Theodolua,

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.830
so isn't that where <i>Black Nine</i> is?

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.200
Which means...

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.040
Hi!

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:41.000
You're... Bitter Sweet.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.870
Were you and I dating at some point?

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.160
Of course n--

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.620
You've got to be way more careful than that.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.870
It's obvious Dorothea's going to attack,

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:58.580
so I thought, "Maybe we can use all the
confusion to make off with <i>Black Nine</i> ."

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.910
Put yourself in my shoes before you
make me come along for the ride.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.540
To the left.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.750
Next is... right.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:30.950
Got it.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:38.500
Still, castles and whatnot sure do
tend to have these secret passages.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:43.750
His Imperial Majesty apparently went
this way when he escaped from Mazria.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.830
Thanks to that, we can achieve our
goal without sending in a large force.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.700
That'd mean lots of troops,
and a cannon bombardment.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:55.200
The damage would be bad,
and it'd turn into a huge production.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.040
Not much time has passed since
the Schwarz Diese incident,

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:01.660
and we'd rather avoid large-scale combat.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:22.120
Yow, this might be too much even
for Lady Sweet, the demon queen.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.450
It's not going to be too easy.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.160
About what we discussed.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:52.080
The religious order called Eins faded into
the shadows of history over 300 years ago.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.040
I turned up some tidbits that suggest,
that's not necessarily the case.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.200
Did fairies come first, or did God?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.000
Did fairies bring forth both God and the world?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.870
Or did God create the world... and fairies?

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:11.620
Which could it have been?

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:15.450
The fairy scholars thought fairies came first.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:19.370
They follow the traditions
of the Eins order, after all.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:25.330
For that matter, Hel S. Bellwood and
the first fairy scholars were Eins itself.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.120
Then you agree, Master Eajey?

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:32.700
I don't care which it is.
Either way, I'll use fairies.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.000
They have endless potential uses.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:41.000
Unified Zesskia is a nuisance, for trying
to wield exclusive control over them.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.250
Master Eajey!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:50.370
Multiple lookouts have been
discovered dead in the city.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.620
Intruders.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.120
Dorothea must be here.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.370
Quatoe.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:59.250
Yes, Master Eajey. I will see to it.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.580
This smell...

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.660
This is the part of the job
that always depresses me.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:41.160
But if the surgery had worked, this guy
would've been another valuable asset.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.450
It might be your turn next.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:46.080
Don't even joke like that.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.500
What's going on here?

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.620
A bone?

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.620
Th-This place is a...

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.250
Let's move on. This place is sickening.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.370
There they are!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.080
Doesn't it feel like they were
already looking for us?

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.290
Did they notice our approach?

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:02.910
We'll deal with this.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.160
Go on ahead!

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.290
All right.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.660
Let's go!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:07.870
Yes, sir.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.660
Welcome, members of Dorothea.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.660
Fairies? <i>Three</i> of them?!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.870
I was ordered by Master Eajey
to give you a warm welcome

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:34.500
using the Cultivated Fairy Soldiers we've produced.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.500
"Gui Carlin mafia group Cultivated Fairy Soldier:

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.500
Cultivated... Fairy Soldiers?!

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:42.700
Another of the same?!

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:48.290
There's a whole bunch of 'em!

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.120
A whole bunch?!

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.450
They're surprisingly tough!

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:07.000
We Cultivated Fairy Soldiers
can be mass-produced.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.540
Amazing, yes?

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.040
Mass-produced?!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.330
There are lots of Fairy Soldiers up above!

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:39.870
Out of the way!

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:45.040
You're nothing but four outdated
pawns of Unified Zesskia!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.080
There's too many of them!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.660
No use in complaining!

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.450
Marlya!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.080
Get this one!

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.750
No way!

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.040
It's not about numbers!

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.790
Must reach Master Eajey...

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.790
Shit! He's getting away!

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.620
Go after him, Free!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.620
We won't be far behind!

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:46.370
You know we believe in you, sir!

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.540
So believe in you guys too, huh?

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:08.700
In the name of duty, we went
to war and shed blood.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.950
I can fight because I have a cause.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.580
But is that really true?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.200
I've found some dear comrades.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.160
I have them. Isn't <i>that</i> why I, too, can fight?

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.250
Master Eajey!

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:32.450
Howl!

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:50.790
Oh, it's you. Where's Nein Auler?

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:54.660
Trembling in her chair, too afraid to face me?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:58.370
Her, afraid? Of the likes of you?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:03.950
Well, if I slaughter all of you,
Auler will have to show up.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:11.870
If I just kill that witch, Unified Zesskia will
fall as if it was built upon Midend's sands.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:15.450
There's no need to trouble the director.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:17.750
I'll just cut you down!

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:19.750
Then, it'll be over.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:24.540
Ah, Verosteal. Free Underbar...

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.950
It's a special occasion. Enjoy!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.750
Not bad at all.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:51.790
Sure enough, I can't see you.
Aren't Fairy Weapons convenient.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.700
Right back at you.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.830
You won't escape!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.080
Don't you find it strange?

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:35.870
Fairies don't rightfully belong to anyone!

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:43.370
You can use a fairy and a Fairy Weapon, so why
are you happy to be Unified Zesskia's pet?!

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.040
Because there are people like you!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.500
If I was king of this land,
I'd set the fairies free.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:52.370
People and fairies would live together,
contending with and killing one another!

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:54.660
It'd be an ideal new world!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:02.330
Did you think bringing a Fairy Weapon
would let you fight on my level?!

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:13.370
Free!

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:18.330
Help has arrived.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:20.830
I'm not as clever as you.

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.160
That's because I'm all-powerful.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.370
Who needs your ideal world?!

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:37.950
I'm tired of hearing about villainous causes!

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:40.330
For my comrades who believe in me...

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.500
...I'm taking you down right here!

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:54.950
Impossible!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:05.120
Who do you think I am?

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.950
Just a loser.

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.660
I'm...

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.370
...not going out with a loss.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.330
Free!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.950
Close call.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.370
I'll say.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.750
With this, at last...

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:37.540
If you would, please.

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:43.290
Then I will head back to Dorothea
HQ first, and deliver <i>Black Nine</i> .

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:45.750
We will mop up the remaining enemies

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:49.870
as we continue our search for the
Fairy Weapon Morterant.

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:53.080
Gui Carlin has been virtually destroyed.

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:55.160
But be careful nonetheless.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:56.540
--Yes, ma'am.
--Yes, ma'am.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:09.370
Do it.

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:29.000
Lily?!

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:30.540
Wolfran Row!

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:37.750
That's... Ozz's fairy?!

00:23:39.370 --> 00:23:42.160
The culprit was using Ozz's fairy.

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:43.790
Elements of the divine beast?

00:23:43.790 --> 00:23:46.580
I'm one of those fairy-possessed?

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.500
"Next time"
"Sad Voices and Black Book"

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:48.500
Soon, it will all be over.
